  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "275082a9-19e8-47ef-afa6-0d3c385300af",
    "name": "Student",
    "description": "## Initial Setup Workflow\n\nTo successfully test the API, please follow these steps in order to maintain referential integrity in the database:\n\n### 1\\. Authentication\n\n- **Endpoint:** `POST /auth/login`\n    \n- **Action:** Log in with your admin credentials to receive your Access and Refresh tokens.\n    \n- **Note:** The system uses secure HTTP-only cookies. Ensure your Postman environment is configured to handle cookies or manually include the `Authorization` header for subsequent requests.\n    \n\n### 2\\. Define School Infrastructure\n\nBefore adding students, you must define the organizational structure:\n\n- **Step A: Create a Section**\n    \n    - **Endpoint:** `POST /sections`\n        \n    - **Payload:** `{ \"name\": \"A\" }`\n        \n    - **Purpose:** Establishes the physical/logical breakout for a grade.\n        \n- **Step B: Create a Class**\n    \n    - **Endpoint:** `POST /classes`\n        \n    - **Payload:** `{ \"name\": \"First grade\", \"sections\": [\"A\"] }`\n        \n    - **Purpose:** Creates the grade level and maps the previously created section to it.\n        \n\n### 3\\. Onboard a Student\n\n- **Endpoint:** `POST /students`\n    \n- **Action:** Use the `class` and `section` names defined in the previous steps.\n    \n- **Validation:** The system will verify that the section exists within the specified class before allowing the creation of the student record.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "14503289"
  },
